  Quote of the Week:

  Pope Julius II, in reply to Michelangelo, who had asked which of his 
artistic tools the Pope would like to try (1506):
  "Nay, give me a sword, for I am no scholar."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  With the advent of the spring season Avalanche prepared to quench his 
thirst for adventure.  He prepared his armies to defend Juneau and the 
surrounding provinces.
  A diplomatic furor erupted between the Realms of Avalanche (whose 
alliances are too incompatible) and Medard (#17), degrading their diplomatic 
relations 1 level(s)!

  Thus endeth the adventures of Lord Avalanche for this year.

  Josh the gentle (#3) Treated with Lord Avalanche, but Avalanche did not 
react to his friendly overtures.  It is hoped that next year, both Kings 
will see the wisdom of Treating.


  Here is the financial report for Avalanche's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  0 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Avalanche was left 
with 0 gold in the treasury.


